{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-23 19:25:45 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-24 02:25:45 +0700 ICT\n\n**REQUEST CHANGES**\n\n**P1 resolved.** Both free-name scanners now belong to `yin.vm.debruijn-linker`, appear in its export list, and fit the B6 file box’s “Existing edits: none” boundary.\n\n**P2 partially resolved.** The R5 phase box now assigns register linking to B6 and names only the unified linker files. Three remaining statements in the register design still imply a separate R5 deliverable: “[R5] or B6 linker” at [line 674](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:674), “R5 together with B6, depending on … B6” at [line 1008](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1008), and “if R5 is commissioned” at [line 1106](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1106).\n\n**P2 | Recommendation:** Revise those statements to treat register linking as scope delivered by B6. The revised [phase box](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1011) and linker design can then give implementers one consistent milestone contract. No files were edited."}}
